> A lot of them do, yes, but sometimes you get lucky.

(From code inspection a couple years ago) I seem to recall
(CMIIW) that once below a certain HP value they quaff their
potion(s) with a 50% probability each turn. That magnitude
would also match with my observation quite well. The more
damage (melee, missile, spell) you can deal per turn the
more likely it is to get intact potions from the monster's
remains. Which means that it's to some degree indeed luck,
but on average the tougher damage dealing characters will
get more that the wimpier ones.

> [...]  For some reason I usually do not find potions of
> polymorph even in the late game.

This potion has lowest random generation probability (1%,
together with potion of full healing and potion of acid)
and will not be in monsters' equipment. The late game is
often dominated by monster equipment, stuff that monsters
carried, but failed to use in time; this is where we see
those huge stacks.

